  "articles": [
    {
      "sequence_id": 1,
      "text": "2. Answers to questions about the location of a place\n\nWhen you ask Depaato wa doko desu ka? OR Depaato wa doko ni arimasu ka? some Japanese may answer in the following way:\n\nDepaato wa (place) desu/ni arimasu.\n\nIn ordinary conversation, however, the answer is usually simplified to:\n\n(place) desu/ni arimasu.\n\nThe following are some examples:\n\nQuestion: Amerika Taishikan wa doko desu ka?/ni arimasu ka?\n          Where is the American Embassy (located)?\n\nAnswer:   Akasaka desu/ni arimasu.\n          (It's) in Akasaka."
    }
